	(text "X201 50.000 MHz CMOS oscillator (ECS-2520MV-500-BN-TR: +/-50 ppm, -40 to +85 C, 8.0 mA max at 3.3 V)\n-> R209 -> PCLKT0_1 (pin 128; FPGA-TN-02154 section 13: single-ended clocks on PCLKT pins only).\nSupply filter per FPGA-TN-02154 Figure 13.1: FB201 600 ohm bead, C225 0.1 uF, C226 1 uF on VDD_OSC.\nOE (pin 1) tied to VDD_OSC: always running (>= 0.7 Vdd = active). 15 pF maximum load per the data sheet."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 431.8 213.36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2d7f1794-4725-5f3f-8c10-d118076bffbe")
	)
	(text "CONFIGURATION (FPGA-TN-02154 section 6, Table 6.1, Figure 6.1): PROGRAMN, INITN, DONE kept as\nconfiguration pins (SYSCONFIG SDM_PORT=PROGRAMN_DONE_INITN), 4.7k pull-ups to VCCIO0. JTAG port enabled.\nJTAGENB: no signal (C-19), 1k pull-up = JTAG mode, so JTAG stays available whatever the bitstream.\nTCK 4.7k pull-down; TMS, TDI, TDO 4.7k pull-ups. SN (pin 70) carries SA17, an FPGA output: 4.7k\npull-up to VCCIO2 keeps SN high while the device is erased (\"ensure SN and PROGRAMN are not driven low\")."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 304.8 104.14 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4e2fa0ee-12ed-58b9-afbe-3b168e767eef")
	)
	(text "J201 JTAG (programming and boundary scan): VREF = carrier +3V3, so a programmer\nnever powers the board. The RP2040-driven JTAG option (D-12) joins these nets on sheet 4\nthrough a translator whose enable is a DIP switch (sheet 6)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 330.2 175.26 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "556f2ea2-b54b-5083-8527-9d97e1fd4c5c")
	)
	(text "DECOUPLING (Lattice FPGA-TN-02154 Table 3.1): VCC 2 x 10 uF + 100 nF per pin (4 pins);\nVCCIO 10 uF per bank + 100 nF per pin (12 pins, 6 banks). 100 nF at each pin on the PCB."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 304.8 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a9e0eca5-7c02-59d4-8a3b-49dca9d5b806")
	)
	(text "DESIGN NOTES (summary; full analysis in docs/stage2/sheet2-design-notes.md)\n1. Every signal pin comes from tools/fpga/pinplan.py (also the LPF LOCATEs and docs/stage2/sheet2-pin-assignment.md).\n   Bank 1 holds the whole /SLAVEn, XRDY and buffer-enable decode group (C-01/C-02 paths).\n2. Owner decision C-17: 102 signals; PROGRAMN/INITN/DONE and JTAG kept; JTAGENB unused (C-19); 2 spare (pins 23, 24).\n   Fallback LCMXO2-4000HC-4TG144C: every assigned pin is an I/O in the same bank, and the configuration, JTAG, SN,\n   PCLKT0_1 and I2C pins are the same package pins (checked by tools/fpga/pinplan.py against the 4000 pinout file).\n3. Post-place-and-route STA at these pins (both grades, 15 pF): every constraint met; worst Zorro path 15.09 ns of 18;\n   /SLAVEn at the slot 20.7 ns of 35 (docs/stage2/sheet2-sta-results.md).\n4. Interfaces: sheet 1 (ZB_*, ZF_*, EN_OK, LD*), sheet 3 (SA*, SRAM_*, LD*), sheet 4 (RP_*, FPGA_TCK/TMS/TDI/TDO),\n   sheet 5 (I2C_*, INA_ALERT_N, X4_*), sheet 6 (LED_*, DIP_*, DBG*). Sheets 4-6 are not yet drawn.\n5. Erased-device rules (FPGA-TN-02155 section 6): the I2C configuration port on pins 125/126 ACKs 7-bit\n   addresses 0x40-0x43, so no telemetry device on I2C_SDA/I2C_SCL may use them (sheet 5). SN is never driven low.\n   SDA/SCL are limited to -0.25..3.75 V (data sheet Table 3.1 note 5): I2C pull-ups to +3V3 only.\n6. Back-powering (FPGA-TN-02154 section 14): no FPGA input may be driven while +3V3 is off. Sheets 1 and 3 comply\n   (Ioff / VCC-isolated buffers, pull-ups to +3V3); sheets 4-6 must keep this rule (debug header, X4 sense lines).\n7. Not yet validated: an ERC-clean result does not imply electrical or timing correctness."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 355.6 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bb884fb2-2af8-5d66-ab13-695cac94fe29")
	)
	(text "POWER (data sheet Table 3.2: HC core VCC 2.375-3.6 V, VCCIO 1.14-3.6 V): VCC and every VCCIO bank on the\nsame +3V3 supply (Table 3.2 note 1: like supplies tied together); all banks LVCMOS33. Sheet 5: ramp 0.01-100 V/ms\n(Table 3.3); regulator within 3% (FPGA-TN-02154 section 2.2).\nNC pins 31, 63, 103, 129 not connected (pinout file). On the LCMXO2-4000HC fallback, pins\n31, 63, 103 are I/O pads (MachXO2-4000 pinout): unconnected here, so no change is needed."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 172.72 264.16 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bfc982c8-2d94-59d1-b095-5f44c231e92d")
	)
